WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.230
We're thinking of singing 
"Dis one." as our last song.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.910
You mean Zero's big hit?

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.820
You're going to cover it?

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.530
Who do you think wanted you to sing the most?

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.360
Who made you this sad?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.990
What can I do?

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.050
<b>Achimochii i7 Iorin Love
Got my nails done for the i7 concert [happy] Iorin color ♥️</b>

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.990
<b>i7 Account_Looking for solace 
The world of i7 is exhausting these days so 
I'm taking a break from social media</b>

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.770
I'm home...

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.680
Iori?

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.300
I'm home!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.100
Nii-san?

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.090
Welcome back.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.160
Iori, are you hungry?

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.640
Want me to make some pancakes?

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.060
Pancakes, you say?

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.950
Yeah. With plenty of honey, 
just the way you like them.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.070
Made by me, your talented 
pastry chef and brother.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.200
Thank you. I love your pancakes.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.870
I know. It's your reward for working so hard.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.740
You're a good boy.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.500
You're juggling both work and school, 
and you're always helping everyone out.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.490
I'm proud to call you my brother.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:08.410
Nii-san...

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.580
Since you can do everything,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.720
awkwardness within the group hurts 
more than being compared to them.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.540
But hey, I understand Riku's depression, too.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.140
So wait for him to get better, all right?

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:26.450
I will.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.510
Don't worry. I'll add buttercream, too.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.980
I'll put whatever you want on them.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.780
What do you want? Tell me.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.450
After all, they're special pancakes for you.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.450
Could you make them bear-shaped?

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.960
Sure. I'll do my best to make bear 
pancakes that'll cheer you up.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.780
It's okay. I'm sure everything will be fine.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.460
Both the pancakes and us.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.590
We'll be all right, for sure.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.450
Discover...

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.480
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.670
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:17.690
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.030
Wow...

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:33.670
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:38.760
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.510
No matter what tomorrow's 
like, it won't betray us

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.990
We'll change even the 
harshest environments

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.860
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.400
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.650
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.410
Discover...

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.410
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.830
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.170
Night sky

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.310
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.510
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:24.140
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.430
Wow...

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.990
#08 I Want You to Know!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:50.370
Allow me to introduce the guests 
we've been waiting for, Re:vale!

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.330
Good evening.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.310
Everyone's talking about Re:vale,

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.840
whether it's about covering Zero's hit 
song or your fifth anniversary concert.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.040
Well? How are you feeling?

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.600
Nervous, but also excited.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.720
I love trying new things!

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.630
Momo-kun, you're always so cheerful.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.120
Yuki-kun, how about you?

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.270
The pressure would've been intense 
if I were alone, but I've got him.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.380
You guys always seem so close.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.560
We even bathe together.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.900
No, we don't.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.570
We have his and his chopsticks.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.100
But we don't know each other's full names.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.990
Or the name of our group.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.730
<i>That </i>you should remember.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:35.670
Comedy couple Re:vale, 
please get ready to go onstage.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.030
Okay!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.460
<b>Filming In Progress</b>

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.360
Okay, cut.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.170
<b>Filming In Progress</b>

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.000
Re:vale is amazing.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.510
They've been top idols forever 
and care for each other so much.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:53.730
You're right. And they always 
relieve any tension around them.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.450
Um...

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.480
Nanase-san, go ahead.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.110
No, you first.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.270
What's up with them?

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.970
Focus.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.160
Mikki.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.670
Nagicchi.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.710
So-chan—

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:14.970
Wait!

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.620
<i>What's wrong, Momo-kun?</i>

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.130
Momo?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.580
I can't...

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.300
I'm trying to sing, but I can't.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:37.030
I can't believe the winners of 
<i>Black or White</i> had to lip sync.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.810
I hope Momo-san just 
isn't feeling well today.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.420
But for him to lose the ability 
to sing, now of all times?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.820
It's as if Zero doesn't want 
his song to be covered.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.950
"Get back my song..."

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.900
Give me back my song?

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.830
<b>Re:vale Green Room</b>

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.270
Momo.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.650
See? You heard that, right?

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.370
I can speak. I can even shout.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:12.200
But when I try to sing, it feels 
like my throat is blocked.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.780
I wonder why...

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.270
It's okay. They can fix that at the hospital.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.300
Should I see a throat specialist?

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.150
I can speak normally, though.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.650
And a psychosomatic specialist.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:26.990
Why? I'm happy! I'm not 
worried about anything.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.360
Look, funny faces!

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.250
Momo!

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.280
I'm sorry for all the trouble I'm causing.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:36.890
It's okay.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.910
What if I don't regain the ability to sing?

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:43.830
It'll be okay. Trust me.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.800
Yuki...

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.560
Yeah.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.650
Yuki, you're so handsome...

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.510
I know.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.220
Yeah.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.560
I wonder what's wrong with Momo-san.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.970
I hope it's not serious.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.310
Did you hear about the 
graffiti on the street?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.240
It could be that.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.730
You know, "Get back my song."

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.010
Maybe it's demanding
 the return of Zero's song.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:13.650
Re:vale is popular, but they're 
still suffering pushback.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:17.600
What we deem precious, what we deem
important, and what we want to protect...

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.620
It's different for everyone.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:26.250
What do people want from IDOLiSH7?

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.530
For you to return to the center position.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.170
That's not true.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.140
Lots of people prefer you, Iori.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.260
Maybe it's better if I'm not the MC.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.970
What are you talking about?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.640
No one here is a better 
conversationalist than you.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.560
That's right, Mitsuki.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.400
But it's not what the fans want.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.820
In that case, they don't want me, either.

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:00.330
We should be doing what we can.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.030
Nobody wanted MEZZO" when they 
first debuted, either. Remember?

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.810
But it's working out.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.920
We made it this far.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.480
You're doing great.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.480
Here.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.640
Thank you.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:23.550
A lot of the boys seem down recently.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.310
MEZZO" seems to have improved, though.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.560
You're right.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.830
The single is selling well, and their 
namesake show is doing well, too.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.990
Haven't they received other offers?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:34.910
Yes.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.750
A variety-style school drama, a namesake 
talkshow for another station,

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.410
and all these offers to appear 
as guests on popular programs.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.490
We're receiving tons of fan 
letters and mail, too, but...

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.970
They're all serious boys at heart.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:52.520
Perhaps they're more strongly 
influenced by demands.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:56.790
Before, all of them were forward-facing.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.000
But now, out of consideration 
for each other's fans,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.210
it feels like they're 
reluctant to step forward.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.670
I have to support them.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:05.310
What?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:09.910
Momo-san told me that this is
 the most important time for them.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:13.130
It's nobody's fault,
but groups still fall apart.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.170
He's right.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.370
The truth is, they know.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:21.010
They know they're all doing their best.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.500
They know everyone's performing 
to the best of their ability.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:30.220
Their efforts have paid off in the form of 
tons of fans, but their confidence is gone.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.570
They're anxious.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.060
And what they need now,
the most important thing is...

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.760
Well, you already know, don't you?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:38.840
Yes.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.820
I'm going to give them one 
yes to beat a million no's.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:48.730
<i>For example, even if there's only one 
person in my class who doesn't like me,</i>

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.730
<i>I become afraid to enter the classroom.</i>

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.840
Thanks for today, everyone!

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:53.740
Thank you!

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.870
I saw Tenn-kun up close.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:10:27.170
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.480
I'm so happy.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.070
I bet Kujo Tenn is picky when it 
comes to his fans, though.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:05.050
He was standing by the same fans forever.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:09.250
<b>Ryunosuke
 LOVE</b>

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.950
Probably because he's young.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.250
Ryunosuke-san is nice to everyone.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.250
Tenn, are you okay?

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.380
I'll tape that for you.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.870
Thank you.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:19.640
Sorry for taking up your time.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.220
No, we're sorry.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:23.340
<i>Nobody's at fault.</i>

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.390
You injured yourself on the scaffolding.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.820
<i>They just want to protect what they love.</i>

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.170
No, I was careless.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:34.140
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.560
Our fans are waiting. Let's go.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:32.260
<i>But idols stand on the front lines.</i>

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>They try to respond to everyone's desires.</i>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.180
Momo-kun was a little mean tonight.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:43.000
He kept forcing the newbie 
to join the conversation.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.080
I like him when he's nice.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.500
I like Momo-chan when he's pushy, though!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.080
I felt bad for the newbie, but as long 
as Momo-chan's cute, I don't mind.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.900
I'm sorry, Momo-san!

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.710
I was able to speak during rehearsal, 
but my head went blank during the show.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:00.210
It happens.

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:04.300
Sorry I kept talking to you. 
I thought it might work.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.510
But thanks to you, it was a ton of fun!

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:09.260
<i>Because they can make people happy,</i>

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.120
It's okay, really.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:13.280
<i>all the voices surrounding IDOLiSH7,</i>

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:17.230
<i>all the love, hate, expectations, 
and dissatisfaction...</i>

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.530
<i>They accept all of it and charge ahead.</i>

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:24.000
<i>So I need to tell them in 
the loudest voice possible</i>

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.510
<i>those important words that 
mean both "Do your best!" and</i>

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:31.440
<i>"You don't have to try so hard."</i>

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.540
<i>Because now is the time.</i>

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.760
I love IDOLiSH7!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.760
IDOLiSH7 is the best idol group!

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.350
Where did that come from?

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:52.250
I'm a huge fan of IDOLiSH7.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:58.050
Your smiles, your songs, and your 
dancing always bring me happiness.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.360
Thank you so much!

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.030
Manager?

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.220
Iori-san!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:05.840
Iori-san, you've been hugely 
successful as the center.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.480
Everyone is delighted.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:08.870
Uh, okay...

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.090
Yamato-san, even though you're 
busy with your acting jobs,

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:14.960
thank you for supporting everyone.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:16.420
Sure...

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:20.330
Mitsuki-san, thanks to you, 
everyone loves the show.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:22.220
It's extremely fun to watch!

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.380
Th-Thanks...

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:27.690
Tamaki-san, all the staff were praising you.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.770
They said you're easier to talk to now.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.310
Uh, thanks...

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:37.690
Sogo-san, every station appreciates your 
ability to handle all kinds of difficulties.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.690
Thank you, too.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:40.790
Nagi-san,

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:44.750
both the staff and other personalities 
are captivated by your chaotic charm.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.580
Thanks. I'm captivated by you, too.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:52.700
Riku-san, your singing voice 
is the best in the world.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:58.380
Even if the group changes, it's not truly 
IDOLiSH7 without you as the center.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.000
Thank you.

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:06.110
I'll say it again: IDOLiSH7 
is the best idol group!

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:10.080
Since the day you guys played basketball 
here, I've always supported you.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.930
So believe in yourselves!

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:17.400
IDOLiSH7 would be incomplete if any 
one of you were missing or replaced!

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:21.020
It's perfect with the seven of you!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:26.830
Hold your heads high. Be proud.
Be the IDOLiSH7 you know you are!

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:30.700
Forever and ever and ever,

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.580
I look forward to working with you!

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.940
Yes!

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:47.720
All right! Let's keep practicing!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.330
Yeah!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:59.250
I'm glad. Everyone's smiling.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.750
You're right.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.910
Sir, you're here?

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.650
I was worried.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.900
After all, they're our crown jewel.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:12.030
They're the special feast we 
prepared with our heart and soul.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:16.440
Their manager reminded them 
of that before they went bad.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:22.920
Little by little, they'll learn on 
their own how to face the world.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:29.160
The manager was amazing.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.890
Maybe she realized something was going on.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.270
Probably.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.120
Mitsu, I've got something for you.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.140
Put out your hand.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.010
What?

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:39.940
Here.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:44.770
It's nothing.

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.490
It's moderation.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.550
You taught me what it means 
to give everything I've got.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:56.640
So I'm teaching you what moderation means.

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:57.920
Yamato-san...

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.180
Sometimes it's okay to be just okay.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:02.110
You don't have to try so hard.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.950
I like you best the way you are.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:06.960
Where is this coming from?

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:08.750
I couldn't help it.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:12.640
We're the only ones who knew you 
were crying in the bathroom.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:16.650
There are things that people who only 
ever see you smile can't understand.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.010
Idiot...

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.650
This isn't like you.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.250
You're right.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.390
I'll hold on to this moderation, then.

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:34.790
Why? I gave it to you to use.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.310
You should use it.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:42.060
No, I'll save it for when I really
 can't take it anymore.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.810
When I think of it that way, 
I feel like I can keep trying.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.830
I... I can keep trying.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.430
Rokuya-san.

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.600
What is it?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:59.170
I keep hearing coughing coming 
from Nanase-san's room.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.560
Could you take this to him?

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:06.890
You saved me with your words once before.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.090
Could you please cheer up Nanase-san?

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:14.240
Seeing my face might cause him 
unnecessary concern again.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:18.610
No, that's not my job.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:20.450
Iori, you should take it to him.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:21.910
Rokuya-san...

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.460
Riku is waiting.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.100
Um...

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.720
Nanase-san...

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.690
I've been looking things up online.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.850
I couldn't understand it on my own.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.050
What?

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.810
What would you like as thanks
 for being the center?

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:42.490
What?

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:53.370
On my way home the other day, a stranger
 asked me to shake their hand.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.260
Huh? What did you do?

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.910
I shook their hand.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.380
Then they looked at my 
face and started crying.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.790
They said they were happy.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.980
Meeting you must've been 
a moving experience.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:10.910
They said they were glad to see 
me working so hard these days.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:16.090
The other day when you said you were happy,

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:20.060
when you got angry on my behalf 
when my dad appeared on that show,

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:22.240
when that person cried...

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:25.160
It all kind of felt the same.

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:28.310
I'm not sure how to describe it, though.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.710
It felt like people were watching me.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.380
Not just looking at me normally, but...

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:38.060
Ah, how should I put it?

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.990
Sort of like we've always been 
connected, or something.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.540
I see.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:47.710
What?

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:50.330
Since I've always had people watching me,

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:53.470
I wasn't very good at 
getting angry or crying.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.590
But you were the opposite.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.180
The opposite?

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.040
You didn't have anyone watching over you—

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.900
at least, you thought you didn't—

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:04.690
so you had to yell and get 
angry on your own behalf.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.550
I'm watching you.

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:13.660
When you're in pain or frustrated, you 
don't have to get angry on your own.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.150
There are lots of people who 
understand how you feel.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.320
You have people watching over you.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.320
So-chan...

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.470
I promise you this.

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:28.500
Even if your voice is softer than 
pianissimo, I'll do my best to notice.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:32.500
If you're unhappy, I'll get upset first.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.380
You don't have to raise your fists anymore.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:37.340
I see.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.450
Yeah.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:40.880
What about me?

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:41.560
Huh?

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.890
What should I do for you?

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:50.070
Well, I'm better at getting 
angry than I was before,

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.460
but I'm over 20 and still 
can't cry in front of people.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.570
I guess it would be crying 
for me when I'm sad.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.400
Got it. I'll do it!

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.160
Thanks.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:13.460
Good evening. Did you forget something?

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.530
You're still working?

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.080
Yes. I'm still working on these documents.

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.780
Thanks for always working so late.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.350
Tamaki-san?

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:29.210
You're working hard for us all the time,

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.100
and I've been watching.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:33.610
I'll keep watching, too.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:37.110
Thank you for your hard work.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:38.500
You're welcome!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.810
Good morning!

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.430
Good morning.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.770
Tamaki-kun, you've really 
pulled it together recently.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:53.830
Thanks.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.440
Good morning.

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:12.230
Jeez. I wish they wouldn't let violent 
people wander around the station.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.430
You're an entertainer.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:17.520
At least have the nerve to shed some 
tears when you see your parent.

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:21.510
I'm an entertainer, too.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:23.880
What should I cry about?

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:28.750
I'm joking.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.300
Well, excuse me...

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:31.120
Goodbye.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:34.340
People really like you these days.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:36.060
I'm relieved, too.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:36.670
Huh?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:40.220
That program forced you to meet 
a relative you don't like

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:41.360
and expected you to smile.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:43.590
It's not a very nice show.

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:46.570
I'm the one who said I'd do it.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.090
It's my fault.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:51.930
But... I think I'd laugh now.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:55.650
There are people who are happy 
to see me behaving properly.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.420
I see.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.110
It's a tough world out there. Good luck.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.170
Right. I'll do my best.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.350
<i>I wonder if Aya has anyone.</i>

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.520
<i>Someone to praise her when she does well.</i>

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.830
<i>Someone who gets angry when she's hurt.</i>

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:15.170
<i>Someone to watch over her like family.</i>

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:22.500
<i>If Aya's alone, I'd tell her 
I'll watch over her from now on.</i>

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:25.170
<i>That I'll watch over her forever.</i>

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.830
I'm back.

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:33.080
Welcome back, Tenn.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:37.540
Your joint practices with 
IDOLiSH7 are starting soon.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:38.440
Yes.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:42.220
Re:vale's new song has caused quite a stir.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:44.330
Covering Zero's song, huh?

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.460
The legendary idol Zero.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:52.470
The people of this country are far too 
attached to that lost false image.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.950
Come here, Tenn.

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:55.880
Okay.

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:06.040
You will shine the brightest 
at the inaugural event.

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:12.220
Even if TRIGGER loses to Re:vale or IDOLiSH7,

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:17.080
Kujo Tenn alone must not pale in comparison.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:23.980
You are the talent that will surpass Zero.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:24.980
Yes.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.280
Good boy.

00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:29.990
Let's eat. Prepare something for us, Aya.

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:32.490
Yes, Father.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:45.710
We came to understand 
a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:51.930
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.320
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:10.530
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:16.170
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:18.620
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.090
We quietly adorn

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:31.210
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:35.220
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:44.980
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.640 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Something Important"</b>
